Task: The Guild of Mages is developing a new spell system. Your task is to correctly set up the inheritance for the `Fireball` spell. It should inherit properties like name and mana cost from the base `Spell` class and add its own unique `damage` property, while also overriding the `activate` method to describe the fireball's effect.

Submitted code:
```
class Spell {
  constructor(name, manaCost) {
    this.name = name;
    this.manaCost = manaCost;
  }

  activate() {
    return `${this.name} spell is generic activating using ${this.manaCost} mana.`;
  }
}

class Fireball extends Spell {
  constructor(name, manaCost, damage) {
    super(name, manaCost);
    this.name = name;
    this.manaCost = manaCost;
    this.damage = damage;
  }

  activate() {
    return `A fiery ${this.name} bursts forth, dealing ${this.damage} damage using ${this.manaCost} mana!`;
  }
}

```

Does this code correctly implement the inheritance concept? Check for proper OOP usage.
assistant: ```json
{
  "is_correct": false,
  "issues": [
    "Redundant property assignments in subclass constructor"
  ],
  "fixes": [
    "Remove `this.name = name;` and `this.manaCost = manaCost;` from the `Fireball` constructor as `super(name, manaCost);` already handles these assignments."
  ]
}
```

